1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,214
In 2019, a cotton seed
sprouted on the Moon.

2
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:08,210
Then the long lunar night came...
and it froze.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:14,970
Now, at the Moon's south pole, one tiny
mustard flower must survive.

4
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:18,510
Her name is Alo.
In Bangla, Alo means light.

5
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:22,570
We are Team The Last BrainCell,
from Dhaka, Bangladesh.

6
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,997
Our challenge: build a Junior
Astronaut Mission Trainer.

7
00:00:27,037 --> 00:00:31,910
Our answer: Last Light Academy.
Real space science that students can play.

8
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:35,960
Four cadets. Four systems.
One shared mission.

9
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,430
KAI: Power's mine!

10
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:39,530
AMARA: I make the air.

11
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:42,810
MEI: I keep the garden... and Alo.

12
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,030
RAFI: And I guard the Safe Room.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,030
Each cadet holds a secret clue.
Share it, or the plan breaks.

14
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:55,136
Sunlight becomes sun-drops. Plan them,
preview the shift, then commit.

15
00:00:55,176 --> 00:00:57,520
Every choice changes the next one.

16
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:04,271
Air takes power. Crops need light.
The shelter needs shielding.

17
00:01:04,311 --> 00:01:07,010
And everything shares one water supply.

18
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:13,049
Real NASA data drives every mission.

19
00:01:13,089 --> 00:01:16,152
LOLA terrain and JPL Horizons
set the night.

20
00:01:16,192 --> 00:01:18,520
DONKI and CRaTER shape the storm.

21
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:24,380
Earth sets. No signal from home.
Just your team.

22
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:30,330
Then, a real solar storm,
replayed from September 2017.

23
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:32,370
RAFI: This is not a drill!

24
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,340
Move the garden's water into
the shelter, and save the crew.

25
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:43,000
MEI: Now bring that water back to Alo!

26
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:48,650
First Light. Your plan decides
whether Alo blooms.

27
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:57,010
Then the debrief shows every decision,
its outcome, and the science behind it.

28
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:01,480
A purpose to care about:
keep Alo alive.

29
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:05,060
Real mission limits,
from real NASA sources.

30
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,670
Every role matters.
Private clues, shared decisions.

31
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:13,710
Consequences you can see.
Change one choice, compare, explain.

32
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:18,260
Students learn systems thinking:
energy, life support, crops, shielding.

33
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,859
Real astronaut crew skills: communication,
teamwork, decisions under pressure.

34
00:02:22,979 --> 00:02:26,477
And they learn through replay.
Try, compare, improve.

35
00:02:26,597 --> 00:02:31,657
Inspect instruments, operate real systems,
and preview every shift before you commit.

36
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:36,012
Play your way: solo, with family,
or as a whole classroom.

37
00:02:36,052 --> 00:02:38,070
Four role groups, one station.

38
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:42,243
Engineer Mode adds real units.
Accessible controls.

39
00:02:42,283 --> 00:02:43,980
In Bangla and English.

40
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:48,082
N.: If you're hearing this... Alo bloomed.

41
00:02:48,122 --> 00:02:50,520
Good. Now Alo needs a friend.

42
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:55,829
Season One: eight chapters,
eight real events.

43
00:02:55,869 --> 00:03:01,108
Pollination, moonquakes, ice in the dark,
meteor strikes, an eclipse,

44
00:03:01,148 --> 00:03:03,556
a solar storm, and a lost relay.

45
00:03:03,596 --> 00:03:06,350
And one mystery: who left the seeds?

46
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:08,430
Players come to save Alo.

47
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:14,730
They return for hidden clues,
new tools, and the next mission.

48
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:20,290
And four endings to master, with no ads,
no streaks, no daily pressure.

49
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:24,530
Built exactly for the challenge:
life support, power and heat,

50
00:03:24,570 --> 00:03:27,120
food and plants,
radiation protection.

51
00:03:28,350 --> 00:03:31,940
Observe. Plan. Act. Debrief.

52
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:35,317
Free and offline, in Bangla and English.

53
00:03:35,357 --> 00:03:38,890
One projector, a whole class,
four role groups.

54
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:42,370
At the hackathon, we'll build
Chapter One in Godot.

55
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:47,210
FERREIRA: You didn't survive the Moon.
You ran it.

56
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:52,233
Last Light Academy. One flower.
One Moon year.

57
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,800
Eight missions to learn and grow.

